  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2603.11510v1</id>
    <title>Tiny Aya: Bridging Scale and Multilingual Depth</title>
    <updated>2026-03-12T03:53:13Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.11510v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2603.11510v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Tiny Aya redefines what a small multilingual language model can achieve. Trained on 70 languages and refined through region-aware posttraining, it delivers state-of-the-art in translation quality, strong multilingual understanding, and high-quality target-language generation, all with just 3.35B parameters. The release includes a pretrained foundation model, a globally balanced instruction-tuned variant, and three region-specialized models targeting languages from Africa, South Asia, Europe, Asia-Pacific, and West Asia. This report details the training strategy, data composition, and comprehensive evaluation framework behind Tiny Aya, and presents an alternative scaling path for multilingual AI: one centered on efficiency, balanced performance across languages, and practical deployment.</summary>
    <category term="cs.CL" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2026-03-12T03:53:13Z</published>
